   "year": "2014",
   "venue": "Econometrica",
   "coauthors": [],
   "contribution": "Introduces a class of non-homothetic (PIGL) preferences that keep aggregate balanced growth while letting both income and relative-price effects drive the reallocation of spending from goods to services. Quantifies these channels with US data.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
