   "year": "2020",
   "venue": "Journal of Political Economy",
   "coauthors": [
    "Per Krusell"
   ],
   "contribution": "Documents a steady long-run decline in hours worked as productivity rises. Proposes a class of preferences consistent with balanced growth despite falling hours, in which income effects slightly dominate substitution effects. Revisits the King-Plosser-Rebelo restrictions.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
